@@ -70,6 +70,18 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each object to a string with ``str()``, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result followed by ``end``. Here's an example::
+
+    >>> console.out("Hello, World!")
+
+``out`` does not pretty print containers, wrap or crop text, render console markup, or replace emoji codes. Text is written as-is, with no wrapping at the console width.
+
+Highlighting is applied by default, and you can disable it with ``highlight=False``. You can also pass a basic ``style`` which is applied to the output as it is with print.
+
+
